# EtTextCopyButton Component

`EtTextCopyButton` is an app-level compound component used to copy text with visual and haptic feedback.

## Purpose

- Copy arbitrary text to clipboard (via optional `onCopy` or internal `ClipboardService` when `onCopy` is not provided)
- Show success state (check icon) for a configurable duration
- Optionally emit callbacks for success (`afterCopy`) and failure (`onError`)

## Public API

### `EtTextCopyButton` (root)

- Required:
  - `textToCopy: string`
  - `children: ReactNode`
- Optional:
  - `onCopy?: (text: string) => Promise<boolean>` - custom copy implementation; if not provided, the component handles clipboard copy by itself
  - `afterCopy?: () => void` - called after successful copy
  - `onError?: (error: string) => void` - called on copy/callback failure
  - `successDuration?: number` (default `2000`)
  - `haptics?: boolean` (default `true`)
  - `style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle>`
  - `testID?: string`
  - `accessibilityLabel?: string`

### `EtTextCopyButton.Icon`

- Shows `copy` icon by default
- Shows `checked` icon when copied

### `EtTextCopyButton.Text`

- Text wrapper with theme-aware color

## Behavior

1. Press triggers copy: if `onCopy` is provided, calls `onCopy(textToCopy)`; otherwise uses `ClipboardService.copy(textToCopy)` internally.
2. If success:
   - optional haptic feedback
   - `isCopied = true` (check icon)
   - calls `afterCopy?.()`
   - resets success state after `successDuration`
3. If failed/throws:
   - calls `onError?.(message)`
   - keeps non-success state

## Recommended Usage

```tsx
<EtTextCopyButton
  textToCopy={accountNumber}
  afterCopy={() => track('copy_success')}
  onError={(message) => track('copy_failure', { message })}
>
  <EtTextCopyButton.Icon />
  <EtTextCopyButton.Text>{accountNumber}</EtTextCopyButton.Text>
</EtTextCopyButton>
```

## Notes

- When `onCopy` is not provided, clipboard is handled internally via `ClipboardService` (platform-agnostic adapter, requires `EtoroDiCtx` or root DI context)
- Keep analytics/toasts in `afterCopy`/`onError`
- Supports string shorthand children (`<EtTextCopyButton>value</EtTextCopyButton>`)
